  "_what": "ACME Beverages, Kansas City \u2014 the six-station bottling line. This is the reference plant: the one CI replays, the one the demo shows, and the one the honesty scores are measured against.",
  "_why_data": "Until 2026-08-31 this line lived in labs/kepsim/generate_line.py as hardcoded Python. That made it unscoreable \u2014 a scorer needs ground truth it can read, and a scripted event buried in a loop body is not readable. Describing the line as data is what turned 'the MES seems fine' into a number.",
  "_states": "State column values: 0 stopped, 1 running, 2 starved, 3 blocked, 4 down, 5 changeover. Stations sit behind finite buffers, so a 'down' event genuinely starves everything downstream and blocks everything upstream.",
